# D-Card API — cards: direct issue, link, cancel, reinstate (host; committee reads the link)
# Card number NNN-PPPP = guest sequence in the event + random PIN. QR and link tokens are stored hashed + encrypted.


### Setup
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

###
# @name event
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "planKey": "kawaida", "eventTypeKey": "wedding", "title": "Cards demo", "startsAt": "2026-12-12T15:00:00+03:00", "venueName": "Diamond Jubilee Hall", "contactName": "Asha", "contactPhone": "0754123456" }

> {%
  client.global.set("eventId", response.body.id);
%}

###
# @name guest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/guests
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Rehema", "phone": "0713300001", "cardType": "double", "partnerName": "Hamisi", "consent": true }

> {%
  client.global.set("guestId", response.body.guest.id);
%}

### No card yet → 409
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/guests/{{guestId}}/card
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

### Issue the card directly (host)
# pending → issued. Assigns the card number and tokens. Sending comes in phase 03.
# 200 → Card { guestId, status: "issued", cardNumber: "001-4827", cardType, issuedAt, cancelledAt: null }
# 409 not pending or event cancelled · 403 not host.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/guests/{{guestId}}/issue
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

### Card number and link (host, committee)
# 200 → Card + { "link": "<APP_URL>/c/<token>" }. Open the link in a browser to see the guest card page.
# @name card
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/guests/{{guestId}}/card
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

### Card type is fixed after issue → 409
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/guests/{{guestId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cardType": "single" }

### Cancel the card (host)
# Scans show "Card cancelled"; payments are kept. 200 → Card (status cancelled) · 409 already cancelled.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/guests/{{guestId}}/cancel
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

### Reinstate (host)
# Back to issued with the same number and tokens (or pending if it was never issued). 409 if not cancelled.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/guests/{{guestId}}/reinstate
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
